   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>My interpretation of the VCF specification<br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://samtools.github.io/hts-specs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://samtools.github.io/hts-specs/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480075793000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qTcN8XjBtqozgIDIdzm9B\">http://samtools.github.io/hts-specs/</a></div><div><br></div><div>is that there is no &#39;concept&#39; of population in VCF data. This means that there is no possible way to incorporate population data directly into the VCF data. This is why it needs to be added from some other source, as suggested in the link provided by Zhian.</div><div><br></div><div>HTH!</div><div>Brian<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jan 27, 2022 at 7:19 AM Zhian Kamvar &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zka...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
